    "html": "<p>A cylinder sealed by a movable piston contains <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n\"></span> moles of an ideal gas. Initially, the pressure in the cylinder is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"p\"></span> and the volume occupied by the gas is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V\"></span>. The cylinder is opened and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"6.02 \\times 10^{24}\"></span> gas molecules are released. This causes a <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50\"></span> % increase in the volume and a <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50\"></span> % decrease in the pressure in the cylinder. The average kinetic energy of the gas molecules is unchanged. What is the value of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n\"></span>?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"20\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"30\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"40\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"60\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
